# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so
.Python
env/
venv/
ENV/
.venv
*.egg-info/
build/

# Jupyter
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# Environment files (contain credentials)
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local
# Any derivative of .env, including timestamped rotation backups. `.env`
# alone does not match `.env.bak.20260818-154821`, so a backup holding live
# database credentials was untracked but perfectly committable.
.env.*
*.env.bak*

# Generated per-box MCP client config. Written by
# pellier/backend/generate_mcp_config.py from .env, and it carries the account
# id, cluster ARN, and Secrets Manager ARN for whichever account bootstrapped
# the box. Environment-specific and never worth committing.
pellier/config/mcp-server-config.json

# Claude Code worktrees, debug logs, scheduled tasks, and local settings are
# machine-local. Project skills are reviewed source and ship with the workshop.
.claude/*
!.claude/skills/
!.claude/skills/**

# The distractor-inclusive catalog. `seed_pellier_catalog.py` writes it whenever
# distractors are included, it is 13 MB, and nothing reads it from the repository: the
# committed artifact is the 60-row curated CSV. Untracked AND unignored, it lands in the
# next `git add -A` as a 13 MB accident. That nearly happened.
data/pellier_catalog_expanded.csv

# Internal design docs — working notes, not shipping content.
# Written as `docs/*` rather than `docs/`: git cannot re-include a file whose parent
# directory is itself excluded, so excluding the CONTENTS is what makes the negation
# below work at all.
docs/*
# One exception: the handoff source contract is what the next team authors the lab
# guide against, so it ships with the repository rather than living in an ignored
# directory a clone never receives.
!docs/HANDOFF-SOURCE-CONTRACT.md
!docs/MEMORY_SHOWCASE.md
!docs/GOVERNED-DEPLOYMENT.md
!docs/E2E-IDENTITIES.md
# Reviewed curriculum framing and editable architecture assets for the L400 guide.
!docs/L400-SEARCH-RETRIEVAL-BRIEF.md
!docs/WORKSHOP-STORY-ARC.md
!docs/WORKSHOP-TRANSPORT.md
!docs/architecture/
!docs/release-readiness/

